===========================================================================
textlint-rule-preset-ja-technical-writing and its rules
===========================================================================

issen's rules are reimplemented in Rust after the textlint rules listed
below. No JavaScript was copied, but issen reproduces parts of them so that
its output matches textlint's: the diagnostic messages, the morphological
patterns of ja-no-weak-phrase, no-double-negative-ja and no-dropping-the-ra
and the token shape morpheme-match matches them with, the style patterns of
analyze-desumasu-dearu, the sentence boundaries of sentence-splitter, and
the preset's default thresholds. The expected outputs under tests/fixtures
were produced by textlint with these rules. All of it is used under the MIT
